-- title:
--   Torus-shell vanishing and shell functional equation, deep twist
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a nonzero prime ideal of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ and let $w_{2}\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_p)\to\mathbb C$ (the completion $\mathbb Q_p$ being $p$-adic completion of $\mathbb Q$ at $p$) satisfy: $w_2(n(x)g)=\psi_p(x)\,w_2(g)$ for all $x\in\mathbb Q_p$ and $g$, where $n(x)=\begin{pmatrix}1&x\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$ and $\psi_p$ is the standard local additive character `psiLocal`; right invariance $w_2(gk)=w_2(g)$ for all $k$ in [`AdelicDock.localLevelOne`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L178) at $p$ for the ideal $p^{c}$, i.e. all $k$ whose image under the embedding of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_p)$ into $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles (identity away from $p$) lies in the finite-adelic level-one subgroup of level $p^{c}$; and $w_2\neq 0$. Let $\omega\colon\mathbb Q_p^{\times}\to\mathbb C^{\times}$ be a character with $w_2(z\cdot g)=\omega(z)w_2(g)$ for scalar matrices $z$ and $\lVert\omega(\varpi)\rVert=1$ for the distinguished uniformizer $\varpi$, and let $\chi\colon\mathbb Q_p^{\times}\to\mathbb C^{\times}$ satisfy $\lVert\chi(\varpi)\rVert=1$ and `HasConductorExponentAt` with exponent $a$ (trivial on the $a$-th higher unit group, nontrivial on each lower one), with $2c+1\le a$. Let $w_J\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_p)$ have matrix $\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\-1&0\end{pmatrix}$, let $k$ lie in `localLevelOne` for the unit ideal, and let $t\in\mathbb Q_p$. Write $d^{\times}u$ for the measure on $\mathbb Q_p^{\times}$ obtained by pulling back $\lvert x\rvert^{-1}\,d\mu(x)$ (restricted to $x\neq0$) along $u\mapsto u$, $\mu$ being the self-dual Haar measure at $p$, and set, for $n\in\mathbb Z$, $c_n=\int_{\lvert u\rvert=1}w_2(\mathrm{diag}(\varpi^{n}u,1)\,n(t)\,k)\,\chi(u)\,d^{\times}u$ and $d_m=\int_{\lvert u\rvert=1}w_2(\mathrm{diag}(\varpi^{m}u,1)\,w_J\,n(t)\,k)\,(\chi\omega)^{-1}(u)\,d^{\times}u$. The conclusion is that $\chi\omega$ also has conductor exponent exactly $a$, and that there are integers $n_1,n_2$ with $c_n=0$ for $n<n_1$ or $n>n_2$, with $d_m=0$ for $m<-n_2-2a$ or $m>-n_1-2a$, and with $$(\chi\omega)(\varpi)^{-m}\,d_m=\varepsilon(\chi\omega)\,\varepsilon(\chi)\,\chi(\varpi)^{-m-2a}\,c_{-m-2a}\qquad\text{for all }m\in\mathbb Z,$$ where $\varepsilon(\cdot)=$ `stdRootNumberAt` is the standard local epsilon factor at $s=1/2$ attached to $\psi_p$ and the self-dual measure.
--
--   This is the local functional equation for the twisted torus shells of a Whittaker function fixed by a level-$p^{c}$ group, twisted by a character of conductor exponent $a>2c$ (the "deep twist" regime), in the form used in the local theory of Jacquet–Langlands for $\mathrm{GL}_2$: the shells have finite support on each side and the $w_J$-shells are expressed through the shells of the function itself with the product of two local root numbers as constant. It is used by the corresponding statement for elements of the group generated by such level subgroups.
